[[" xe", -0.00017555108934175223], [" Xe", -9.421154022216797]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -0.2555919289588928, "top": [[" |", -0.2555919289588928], ["\n", -1.6505733728408813]]}, {"t": " grep", "lp": -0.04443897679448128, "top": [[" grep", -0.04443897679448128], [" less", -3.3266313076019287]]}, {"t": " c", "lp": -0.09635265171527863, "top": [[" c", -0.09635265171527863], [" -", -2.414299964904785]]}, {"t": "cs", "lp": -0.00010777100396808237, "top": [["cs", -0.00010777100396808237], ["cc", -10.197800636291504]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.6351675987243652, "top": [["\n", -0.6351675987243652], ["_mode", -0.767089307308197]]}, {"t": "d", "lp": -1.0368874073028564, "top": [["d", -1.0368874073028564], ["#", -1.3898117542266846]]}, {"t": "mes", "lp": -0.0008499657269567251, "top": [["mes", -0.0008499657269567251], ["mod", -8.209623336791992]]}, {"t": "g", "lp": -2.0861843950115144e-05, "top": [["g", -2.0861843950115144e-05], ["n", -12.616487503051758]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -9.382211283082142e-05, "top": [[" |", -9.382211283082142e-05], [" ", -10.515914916992188]]}, {"t": " grep", "lp": -0.0035600177943706512, "top": [[" grep", -0.0035600177943706512], [" c", -6.5021867752075195]]}, {"t": " xe", "lp": -0.48290714621543884, "top": [[" xe", -0.48290714621543884], [" -", -0.9652374982833862]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.3312147557735443, "top": [["\n", -0.3312147557735443], ["  ", -1.749292254447937]]}, {"t": "```", "lp": -0.10685289651155472, "top": [["```", -0.10685289651155472], ["cat", -2.4221394062042236]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.2754479944705963, "top": [["\n", -0.2754479944705963], ["\n\n", -1.4255849123001099]]}, {"t": "And", "lp": -0.07364125549793243, "top": [["And", -0.07364125549793243], ["Or", -2.83030366897583]]}, {"t": " consult", "lp": -0.11424756050109863, "top": [[" consult", -0.11424756050109863], [" look", -2.8129589557647705]]}, {"t": " the", "lp": -0.014008310623466969, "top": [[" the", -0.014008310623466969], [" your", -4.992926120758057]]}, {"t": " kernel", "lp": -0.8626840114593506, "top": [[" kernel", -0.8626840114593506], [" latest", -1.9352586269378662]]}, {"t": " docs", "lp": -0.958014726638794, "top": [[" docs", -0.958014726638794], [" source", -1.1827938556671143]]}, {"t": " at", "lp": -0.6411542296409607, "top": [[" at", -0.6411542296409607], [":", -1.302046775817871]]}, {"t": " `", "lp": -0.04404355585575104, "top": [[" `", -0.04404355585575104], [":", -3.396023750305176]]}, {"t": "Documentation", "lp": -0.0323072150349617, "top": [["Documentation", -0.0323072150349617], ["drivers", -4.163473606109619]]}, {"t": "/g", "lp": -0.15348991751670837, "top": [["/g", -0.15348991751670837], ["/admin", -2.4732797145843506]]}, {"t": "pu", "lp": -0.0021794927306473255, "top": [["pu", -0.0021794927306473255], ["fx", -6.771487712860107]]}], "text": "# CCS Mode on Intel Arc (xe driver)\n\nThe `ccs_mode` parameter controls how Compute Slice (CCS) contexts are distributed across the GPU's compute engines. This is set via the `xe` kernel module parameter (e.g., `modprobe xe ccs_mode=1`).\n\n## The Modes\n\n**ccs_mode 0 (default)**\n- Uses a single CCS engine for all compute contexts\n- Simplest configuration, maximum compatibility\n\n**ccs_mode 1**\n- Distributes compute contexts across **multiple CCS engines**\n- Enables better parallelism for compute workloads by spreading load across available compute slices\n- Better for GPU compute tasks that benefit from concurrent execution\n\n**ccs_mode 2**\n- Similar multi-CCS distribution but with a **different affinity/mapping strategy**\n- The exact mapping differs from mode 1 in how contexts are pinned to specific compute slices\n\n## When to Use Mode 4\n\n**ccs_mode 4** is typically used when you want to **isolate or dedicate compute slices** \u2014 often for:\n- **Virtualization / SR-IOV** scenarios where you need to partition compute resources\n- Workloads requiring **guaranteed dedicated compute slices** without contention\n- Scenarios where you want explicit control over which CCS engines serve which contexts\n\n---\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Important caveat:** The precise semantics of these modes have shifted across driver versions, and the `ccs_mode` parameter has been somewhat inconsistently documented. The exact behavioral differences between modes 1, 2, and 4 can vary depending on your specific `xe` driver version and kernel.\n\n**My recommendation:** Check your actual driver version's documentation:\n```bash\nmodinfo xe | grep ccs\ndmesg | grep xe\n```\nAnd consult the kernel docs at `Documentation/gpu"}